{#
Day and week as a time-grid: hours down the side, an event drawn where it is
and as long as it is, and draggable.

Only ever reached from the full calendar page — _grid.html.twig picks between
this and the column list on `isPane`, and the reasoning for that lives there.

Accepts (all from CalendarController::viewData):
  days    array<Y-m-d, list<OccurrenceCluster>>  — the day walk, for the keys
  range   the reader's answer; `grid` holds the placements, `zone` the clock
  view    CalendarView, for the links the day headers carry
  anchor  the date the view is centred on

**Positions come from the server, as percentages.** range.grid is a DayGrid per
day: the all-day clusters lifted out, and the timed ones each carrying top,
height, lane and lanes as fractions of a 24-hour column. Fractions rather than
pixels so the same numbers stay correct at whatever height the column ends up
with, and server-side so the grid is right on the first paint rather than
jumping into place once JavaScript has run — and so a reader with JavaScript off
gets a readable calendar instead of a pile of blocks at midnight. See
DayGridLayout for how the lanes are assigned and what DST does to the axis.

**Every time printed here names its zone explicitly.** Twig's date filter
defaults to the server's zone, and the placements were computed against the
calendar's — an hour label drawn on one clock over blocks positioned on another
is the one failure mode of this view that looks completely fine.

**The all-day band is always drawn, even when it is empty.** Showing it only on
weeks that have one makes the grid jump by a row as you page through, and the
row is a permanent part of the axis — it is where "this event has no time" is
expressible at all. It is deliberately not a drop target: dragging a timed event
into it would mean "make this all-day", which is a change of kind rather than of
time, and the editor is where kinds are changed.

Deliberately absent: clicking empty grid space does not create an event. Each
day header keeps the same + button the column list has, which is a real tab
stop; a click-to-create on the background would have to be told apart from the
end of a drag on every pointerup, and drag-to-create is its own piece of work.

**A known limitation, stated rather than hidden: a seven-day week is tight below
about 640px.** The columns divide whatever width there is, so on a phone each is
around fifty pixels and a block says its colour and little else. It is not
solved here because the only fixes are disproportionate — a horizontal scroll
means either three scroll containers kept in step by JavaScript or rewriting the
three grids below as one with sticky rows and a sticky gutter — and the paths a
phone actually takes into the calendar do not hit it: the pane, which is what
opens from the mail, keeps the agenda, and the toolbar's Day view is one tap
away and is a single full-width column. Worth revisiting; not worth guessing at.
#}

{% set dayKeys = days|keys %}
{% set grid = range.grid %}
{% set zone = range.zone %}
{% set today = 'now'|date('Y-m-d', zone) %}
{% set nowMinute = 'now'|date('G', zone) * 60 + 'now'|date('i', zone) %}

{# The time gutter, then one equal column per day. minmax(0,1fr) rather than
   1fr: a bare 1fr floors at the content's min-width, so one long untruncated
   title would push a seven-day week wider than the pane and produce a
   horizontal scrollbar over the whole calendar. #}
{% set columnTemplate = '3.5rem repeat(' ~ dayKeys|length ~ ', minmax(0, 1fr))' %}

<div class="h-full min-h-0 flex flex-col"
     data-controller="calendar--time-grid"
     data-action="pointerdown->calendar--time-grid#pointerdown
                  keydown->calendar--time-grid#keydown"
     data-calendar--time-grid-snap-value="15"
     data-calendar--time-grid-read-only-message-value="{{ 'calendar.grid.read_only'|trans }}"
     data-calendar--time-grid-pending-message-value="{{ 'calendar.grid.pending'|trans }}"
     data-calendar--time-grid-reverted-message-value="{{ 'calendar.grid.reverted'|trans }}"
>
    {# ── The day headings ──────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    <div class="shrink-0 grid border-b border-line bg-surface" style="grid-template-columns: {{ columnTemplate }}">
        <div class="border-r border-line" aria-hidden="true"></div>

        {% for dayKey in dayKeys %}
            {% set isToday = dayKey == today %}

            <div class="group/day flex items-baseline gap-1.5 px-2 py-1.5 border-r border-line
                        {{ isToday ? 'bg-accent/5' : '' }}">
                <span class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wide {{ isToday ? 'text-accent' : 'text-ink-faint' }}">
                    {{ dayKey|date('D', zone) }}
                </span>

                {% if isToday %}
                    <span class="w-5 h-5 -my-0.5 flex items-center justify-center rounded-full
                                 bg-accent text-white text-xs font-semibold tabular-nums">
                        {{ dayKey|date('j', zone) }}
                    </span>
                {% else %}
                    <span class="text-sm text-ink-muted tabular-nums">{{ dayKey|date('j', zone) }}</span>
                {% endif %}

                {# One add affordance per day, in the heading rather than 24 of
                   them down the column: a tab stop per hour per day is 168 of
                   them in a week, which makes the grid unusable by keyboard. #}
                <button type="button"
                   data-controller="ui--modal"
                   data-action="click->ui--modal#open"
                   data-ui--modal-src-value="{{ path('app_calendar_event_new', { start: dayKey ~ ' 09:00' }) }}"
                   data-ui--modal-title-value="{{ 'calendar.event.new'|trans }}"
                   aria-label="{{ 'calendar.event.new_on'|trans({ '%date%': dayKey|date('D j M', zone) }) }}"
                   class="ml-auto w-5 h-5 flex items-center justify-center rounded-md text-[10px] text-ink-faint
                          opacity-0 group-hover/day:opacity-100 focus:opacity-100
                          hover:bg-hover transition-opacity
                          focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent"
                ><i class="fa-solid fa-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i></button>
            </div>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>

    {# ── All day ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    <div class="shrink-0 grid border-b border-line bg-surface max-h-24 overflow-y-auto"
         style="grid-template-columns: {{ columnTemplate }}">
        <div class="border-r border-line px-2 py-1 text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wide text-ink-faint text-right">
            {{ 'calendar.grid.all_day'|trans }}
        </div>

        {% for dayKey in dayKeys %}
            <div class="border-r border-line p-1 space-y-0.5 min-h-[1.75rem]
                        {{ dayKey == today ? 'bg-accent/5' : '' }}">
                {% for cluster in grid[dayKey].allDay %}
                    {% include 'calendar/_event_chip.html.twig' with { showTime: false } %}
                {% endfor %}
            </div>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>

    {# ── The hours ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    <div class="flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-y-auto" data-calendar--time-grid-target="scroller">
        <div class="grid" style="grid-template-columns: {{ columnTemplate }}">

            {# The gutter's labels sit ON the hour line rather than inside the
               row below it, which is why they are nudged up by half their own
               height — a "10:00" printed at the top of the 10:00 row appears to
               label the space between 10 and 11. #}
            <div class="border-r border-line">
                {% for hour in 0..23 %}
                    <div class="relative h-12">
                        {% if hour > 0 %}
                            <span class="absolute -top-1.5 right-1.5 text-[10px] tabular-nums text-ink-faint">
                                {{ '%02d:00'|format(hour) }}
                            </span>
                        {% endif %}
                    </div>
                {% endfor %}
            </div>

            {% for dayKey in dayKeys %}
                {% set isToday = dayKey == today %}

                <div class="relative border-r border-line {{ isToday ? 'bg-accent/5' : '' }}"
                     data-calendar--time-grid-target="column"
                     data-day="{{ dayKey }}">

                    {% for hour in 0..23 %}
                        <div class="h-12 border-b border-line/50" aria-hidden="true"></div>
                    {% endfor %}

                    {% if isToday %}
                        {# Rendered at the minute the page was built and never
                           moved afterwards. A timer that crept it down the
                           column would be a repaint a minute forever, on a view
                           that is re-rendered by every navigation anyway. #}
                        <div class="absolute left-0 right-0 h-px bg-danger pointer-events-none z-20"
                             style="top: {{ (nowMinute * 100 / 1440)|round(4) }}%"
                             aria-hidden="true">
                            <span class="absolute -left-1 -top-1 w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-danger"></span>
                        </div>
                    {% endif %}

                    {# The blocks sit in their own layer over the hour lines, so
                       the lines stay visible between and behind them. #}
                    <div class="absolute inset-0">
                        {% for placed in grid[dayKey].timed %}
                            {% set cluster = placed.cluster %}
                            {% set occurrence = cluster.primary %}
                            {% set event = occurrence.event %}
                            {% set readOnly = event.calendar.isReadOnly %}

                            {# min-height is the floor a short meeting needs to
                               be readable. A quarter of an hour is 1/96th of
                               the column — about twelve pixels at the height
                               this grid usually gets — and the chip inside
                               wants twenty-four for one line of "9:00 Standup",
                               so a fifteen-minute event drew a sliver with its
                               own label spilling out of it. 1.75rem is the
                               all-day lane's floor above, deliberately: one
                               number for "the smallest a chip may be drawn".

                               The floored block is then taller than its
                               duration and can reach over the one after it.
                               That is the right trade and not a compromise: the
                               block's TOP is where the meeting starts and stays
                               honest, only the padded bottom is a fiction, and
                               the alternative — reflowing so short events push
                               their neighbours down — would move a 10:00
                               meeting off the 10:00 line, which is the one
                               thing a time grid exists to get right. The
                               overlap is drawn under the later block, because
                               they are emitted in start order and the fiction
                               is what gets covered.

                               Presentational only. The drag reads
                               data-starts-at and data-ends-at, never the
                               rendered box, so a floored block resizes from its
                               real duration. #}
                            <div class="absolute p-px"
                                 style="top: {{ (placed.top * 100)|round(4) }}%;
                                        height: {{ (placed.height * 100)|round(4) }}%;
                                        min-height: 1.75rem;
                                        left: {{ (placed.lane * 100 / placed.lanes)|round(4) }}%;
                                        width: {{ (100 / placed.lanes)|round(4) }}%;"
                                 data-calendar--time-grid-target="block"
                                 data-event-id="{{ event.id }}"
                                 data-recurring="{{ event.isRecurring ? 'true' : 'false' }}"
                                 data-read-only="{{ readOnly ? 'true' : 'false' }}"
                                 {# Wall time on the GRID's clock, which is the clock
                                    the drag is measured against and the one the move
                                    route reads the answer back in. #}
                                 data-starts-at="{{ occurrence.startsAt|date('Y-m-d\\TH:i:s', zone) }}"
                                 data-ends-at="{{ occurrence.endsAt|date('Y-m-d\\TH:i:s', zone) }}"
                                 data-instance="{{ occurrence.recurrenceId|date('Y-m-d\\TH:i:s\\Z', 'UTC') }}"
                            >
                                <div class="relative h-full rounded-md overflow-hidden
                                            ring-1 ring-line bg-surface shadow-sm
                                            {{ readOnly ? '' : 'cursor-grab' }}"
                                     style="background-color: {{ event.calendar.color }}1a">

                                    {% include 'calendar/_event_chip.html.twig' with { tall: true } %}

                                    {% if placed.continuesBefore %}
                                        <span class="absolute top-0 inset-x-0 h-0.5 bg-ink-faint/40"
                                              title="{{ 'calendar.grid.continues_before'|trans }}"></span>
                                    {% endif %}

                                    {% if readOnly %}
                                        <i class="fa-solid fa-lock absolute top-1 right-1 text-[9px] text-ink-faint"
                                           title="{{ 'calendar.grid.read_only'|trans }}"
                                           aria-label="{{ 'calendar.grid.read_only'|trans }}"></i>
                                    {% else %}
                                        {# Mouse only, and aria-hidden on purpose: the
                                           keyboard route to the same change is
                                           Alt+Shift with the arrow keys on the block
                                           itself, so a focusable grip here would be a
                                           second tab stop for a thing already
                                           reachable. #}
                                        <span class="absolute inset-x-0 bottom-0 h-1.5 cursor-ns-resize
                                                     hover:bg-accent/40"
                                              data-calendar--time-grid-target="grip"
                                              aria-hidden="true"></span>
                                    {% endif %}

                                    {% if placed.continuesAfter %}
                                        <span class="absolute bottom-0 inset-x-0 h-0.5 bg-ink-faint/40"
                                              title="{{ 'calendar.grid.continues_after'|trans }}"></span>
                                    {% endif %}
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        {% endfor %}
                    </div>
                </div>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    </div>

    {# ── What the grid says back ───────────────────────────────────────── #}

    {# One hint, referenced by every block, rather than a title on each: the
       instructions are the same for all of them and a screen reader should not
       read them once per event. #}
    <p id="calendar-grid-hint" class="sr-only">{{ 'calendar.grid.keyboard_hint'|trans }}</p>

    {# role="status" rather than a toast. This is about the block the user is
       holding, so it belongs beside it and has to survive being replaced
       several times a second while nudging — a queue of toasts would not. #}
    <p data-calendar--time-grid-target="status"
       role="status"
       aria-live="polite"
       class="sr-only"></p>

    {# ── Committing a move ─────────────────────────────────────────────── #}

    {# A real form submitted by the controller, not a fetch. Turbo then handles
       the answer exactly as it handles the editor's save — a full navigation to
       the redirect, which redraws the grid with the new placements. A fetch
       would need its own re-render path beside the one that already works. #}
    <form method="post"
          action="{{ path('app_calendar_event_move') }}"
          data-turbo-frame="_top"
          data-calendar--time-grid-target="form"
          class="hidden">
        <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('calendar_event_move') }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="timeZone" value="{{ zone }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="view" value="{{ view.value }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="returnTo" value="{{ app.request.pathInfo }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="eventId" data-calendar--time-grid-target="eventIdField">
        <input type="hidden" name="recurrenceId" data-calendar--time-grid-target="instanceField">
        <input type="hidden" name="scope" data-calendar--time-grid-target="scopeField">
        <input type="hidden" name="startsAt" data-calendar--time-grid-target="startsAtField">
        <input type="hidden" name="endsAt" data-calendar--time-grid-target="endsAtField">
    </form>

    {# The same question the editor asks, in the same words, because it is the
       same question — see EventMover. A <dialog> rather than the app's modal
       frame: this one is built from data already on the page and needs no
       fetch, and showModal() puts it in the top layer, which is the one kind of
       dialog backdrop-filter on an ancestor cannot clip. #}
    <dialog data-calendar--time-grid-target="scopePrompt"
            data-action="cancel->calendar--time-grid#cancelPending"
            class="rounded-pane border border-line bg-surface p-0 text-ink backdrop:bg-black/40">
        <div class="px-6 py-4 space-y-3 min-w-[18rem]">
            <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">{{ 'calendar.event.scope.legend'|trans }}</p>

            <div class="flex flex-col gap-1">
                <button type="button"
                        data-action="click->calendar--time-grid#commitInstance"
                        class="px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-sm text-left hover:bg-hover transition-colors">
                    {{ 'calendar.event.scope.instance'|trans }}
                </button>
                <button type="button"
                        data-action="click->calendar--time-grid#commitSeries"
                        class="px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-sm text-left hover:bg-hover transition-colors">
                    {{ 'calendar.event.scope.series'|trans }}
                </button>
            </div>

            <button type="button"
                    data-action="click->calendar--time-grid#cancelPending"
                    class="w-full px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-sm text-ink-muted hover:bg-hover transition-colors">
                {{ 'calendar.event.cancel'|trans }}
            </button>
        </div>
    </dialog>
</div>
